From 70bf1a3f162c02c283fd2c38f3e4f6356163ab0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:15:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/65] Port Save_CharacterRecord (H066+$1640) and its disk
 checks

Port H066+$1640 (body $16EC) with the nested path builder $164E: it
writes name.who (or name.sav) with the $1AA-byte record, name.swg with
the items and name.fx with the effects, after checking the save
directory ($08E4 with $08F2), the free space ($142E) and that the
directory is writable ($14DC with $14EA), and asks before overwriting.
Also port H028+$033E, $07E0 and $08F0 (volume name, file name from the
character name), H030+$028A (message until a key) and the dos.library
wrappers CreateDir, DeleteFile and Examine with host versions; host
Lock now also finds directories and Info reports free blocks.

Pointer fields are written as zero; the original wrote the in-memory
addresses. Create New Character now completes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
